OL,3,GNEWSACould a city get its new 'people's
OL,4,Apool'?
OL,5,
OL,6,FNearly 90 years ago, a busy lido in
OL,7,FBristol's "people's park" was bombed in
OL,8,Fthe Second World War and closed,
OL,9,Fseemingly, forever.
OL,11,FBut for the past seven years a
OL,12,Fcommunity group - the Eastville Park
OL,13,FLido CIC - has been working to bring an
OL,14,Foutdoor pool back to the park and
OL,15,Fchange the narrative that lidos are
OL,16,F"not just for white middle class
OL,17,Fcommunities".
OL,23,APub: 01-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,342,340,200,160,0,100
